---
import LegalPage from "../../../components/app/LegalPage.astro";
import { localizedAlternates } from "../../../core/seo";

const title = "Terms of Use – GiggleFace";
const canonicalPath = "/apps/giggleface/terms-of-use/";
const alternateLocales = localizedAlternates(
    canonicalPath,
    "/pt-br/apps/giggleface/terms-of-use/",
);
---

<LegalPage
    title={title}
    description="Terms of use for GiggleFace."
    lang="en"
    favicon="/apps/giggleface/favicon.png"
    canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
    alternateLocales={alternateLocales}
>
    <h1>{title}</h1>

    <h4>Last updated: August 4, 2026</h4>

    <p>
        These Terms of Use govern your use of GiggleFace on iOS and macOS. By
        downloading or using the app, you agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h3>1. Purpose</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace is a creative camera application that lets users import images,
        create and adjust face masks, apply them to the front camera in real time,
        record videos with audio, share mask files, and provide a virtual camera feed
        to compatible macOS applications.
    </p>

    <h3>2. License and Acceptable Use</h3>

    <p>
        The developer grants you a limited, personal, non-exclusive,
        non-transferable, and revocable license to use GiggleFace on supported Apple
        devices under these terms and Apple's platform rules. The app is provided for
        lawful personal and professional creative use.
    </p>

    <p>
        You may not reverse engineer, copy, modify, resell, rent, or redistribute the
        application or its proprietary assets except where applicable law expressly
        permits it.
    </p>

    <h3>3. Images, Masks, and User Content</h3>

    <p>
        You are responsible for every image, mask, recording, and camera output you
        create, import, display, transmit, or share through GiggleFace. You must own
        the content or have all necessary licenses, permissions, and consents,
        including permission to use another person's image, likeness, or intellectual
        property.
    </p>

    <p>
        GiggleFace does not grant you rights to images obtained from websites, social
        networks, photo libraries, friends, or other sources. Importing an image does
        not remove copyright, privacy, publicity, trademark, or contractual
        restrictions that apply to it.
    </p>

    <h3>4. Prohibited Uses</h3>

    <p>You may not use GiggleFace to create, display, record, or distribute content that:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Is unlawful, fraudulent, deceptive, defamatory, threatening, abusive, or harassing;</li>
        <li>Impersonates another person in a way intended to deceive, defraud, or cause harm;</li>
        <li>Violates privacy, publicity, copyright, trademark, or other rights;</li>
        <li>Contains sexual exploitation, non-consensual intimate content, or any content that endangers minors;</li>
        <li>Breaks the rules of a video-call, messaging, storage, workplace, school, or other third-party service.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You are responsible for making any disclosure required by law, policy, or
        context when a mask or altered camera feed could reasonably mislead others.
    </p>

    <h3>5. Permissions and Recording</h3>

    <p>
        Camera, microphone, photo library, and file access depend on permissions you
        control through iOS or macOS. Some features will not work if the required
        permission is denied. You are responsible for obtaining consent before
        recording or transmitting another person's image or voice and for complying
        with local recording laws.
    </p>

    <h3>6. Virtual Camera and Third-Party Services</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace can provide a virtual camera to macOS apps that support compatible
        camera inputs, including Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, and FaceTime. Support
        can vary by app version, macOS version, hardware, permissions, security
        settings, and service configuration. Compatibility with every service or
        future version is not guaranteed.
    </p>

    <p>
        Third-party communication, sharing, and storage services are independent from
        GiggleFace. Their availability, transmission, recording, moderation, and data
        practices are governed by their own terms and policies.
    </p>

    <h3>7. GiggleFace Premium</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace may be downloaded for free. Custom mask creation and other Premium
        features are unlocked through a single non-consumable in-app purchase. There
        is no recurring GiggleFace subscription for this Premium access.
    </p>

    <p>
        Apple processes pricing, billing, taxes, purchase verification, restoration,
        and refund requests. Restoration requires the Apple ID used for the eligible
        original purchase and depends on Apple's systems. A one-time purchase does not
        guarantee that every feature, third-party integration, or operating-system
        compatibility will remain unchanged indefinitely.
    </p>

    <h3>8. Offline Operation and Connectivity</h3>

    <p>
        Core camera, mask, facial landmark, editor, and recording processing is
        designed to run locally. Internet access may still be required for downloading
        the app, TestFlight, purchases and restoration, importing content from an
        online service, sending anonymous analytics and error diagnostics, sharing
        through online apps, and participating in video calls.
    </p>

    <h3>9. Intellectual Property</h3>

    <p>
        You retain the rights you already hold in your imported images, original mask
        files, and recordings. All rights in GiggleFace itself—including its name,
        design, branding, source code, interface, and included assets—belong to the
        developer and/or Adriano Souza Costa unless otherwise stated.
    </p>

    <h3>10. Performance and Limitation of Liability</h3>

    <p>
        GiggleFace is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without
        warranties of uninterrupted or error-free operation. Recording at up to 60 fps
        depends on supported hardware, selected settings, storage, system load, and
        thermal conditions.
    </p>

    <p>To the extent permitted by law, the developer is not responsible for:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Lost, corrupted, incomplete, or unavailable masks, recordings, or exports;</li>
        <li>Performance limits, overheating, battery use, storage limits, permission errors, or device incompatibility;</li>
        <li>Interruptions or changes made by Apple or third-party communication and sharing services;</li>
        <li>Claims, losses, or disputes resulting from content you create, import, transmit, record, or share.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>11. Updates and Availability</h3>

    <p>
        The developer may update, add, remove, suspend, or discontinue features to
        address security, compatibility, legal, or product requirements. Continued use
        may require a supported version of iOS, macOS, GiggleFace, or a third-party app.
    </p>

    <h3>12. Changes to These Terms</h3>

    <p>
        These Terms may be updated to reflect legal, technical, or product changes.
        Continued use after revised terms become available means you accept the updated
        terms to the extent permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h3>13. Contact</h3>

    <p>
        For questions about these Terms of Use, contact:
        <a href="mailto:adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com">adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
</LegalPage>
